Personality types and health risks:
1. Proneness to cancer: Morris identified Type C personality, characterized by suppression of negative emotions and extreme compliance, predisposing to cancer (A -> IV);
2. Susceptible to CHD: Friedman and Rosenman identified Type A personality (impatience, hostility, time urgency) as susceptible to coronary heart disease (B -> III);
3. Proneness to depression: Denollet characterized Type D personality by negative affectivity and social inhibition, predisposing to depression (C -> II);
4. Relaxed: Type B personality is characterized by an unhurried, patient, and relaxed disposition (D -> I).
This establishes (A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I). (Note: NTA official answer key accepted option matching with full credit).
Hence, option (A) is the correct match.

